 "caveats": [
  "Different clients: ours is reth stateless-validator + revm (Rust, RV64IM) consuming SSZ StatelessInput; ZisK reth guest is reth/revm on ZisK; ziskethone is C++ evmone. Same blocks, same witness.",
  "ZisK STEPS count ZisK ops after transpilation, not RISC-V instructions; ZisK guests are compiled with Zbb/bitmanip and DMA memcpy/memset/memcmp ops, so one step can replace several RV64IM instructions; atomics expand to several steps.",
  "Precompile weight differs: our keccak-f and secp add/double are one retirement each, as are ZisK keccak/secp256k1_add/dbl/arith256_mod; sha256 is software on our side.",
  "Our guest also computes the SSZ new_payload_request hash_tree_root in software sha256 (~10.8% on 24628607); ZisK guests commit the block hash instead.",
  "Steps are a proxy: proving cost per step differs by system (ZisK MAIN cost 68/step; ours per Word16 AIR shape)."
 ]
}
